    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# WordPress AI VoiceOver Workflow\n\n[Full setup documentation: Notion](https://app.notion.com/p/paoloronco/Documentation-WordPress-AI-TTS-VoiceOvers-with-Google-Cloud-3f5f0ba27c3280478f82ccabfa9a0b7c?source=copy_link)\n\n\n## How it works\nThis workflow automatically generates English and Italian voiceovers for WordPress articles.\n\nOn a scheduled run, it:\n1. Fetches recent WordPress posts.\n2. Stores post metadata and content in Google Sheets as a processing queue.\n3. Selects the oldest unprocessed post.\n4. Cleans and normalizes the text (HTML removal, special character cleanup).\n5. Translates the content to English.\n6. Uses Google Cloud Text-to-Speech to generate EN and IT audio files.\n7. Updates dedicated WordPress pages by appending the new audio players.\n8. Marks the processed post as completed in Google Sheets.\n\nThe workflow ensures posts are processed sequentially and avoids duplicates.\n\n## Setup steps\n1. Configure WordPress credentials with read/write permissions.\n2. Create a Google Sheet with columns: ID, Title, Date, Content, Link, Status.\n3. Set up Google Cloud credentials with:\n   - Translate API enabled\n   - Text-to-Speech API enabled\n4. Replace placeholder values (Sheet ID, Page IDs, GCP endpoint URLs).\n5. Adjust the Schedule Trigger if needed.\n6. Run once manually to verify credentials and outputs.\n",
        "height": 720,
        "width": 592,
        "color": 2
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1104,
        -192
      ],
      "id": "1ec5c89c-04b5-4b3f-8fc5-aac9d59bd30b",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
